==German==

===Etymology===
{{calque|de|sauer|Stoff|etyl lang=fr|etyl term=oxygène}}, from Greek-Latin {{m|la|oxygenium||acid-maker}}, due to a mistaken early belief that oxygen was a necessary ingredient in all acids.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈzaʊ̯ɐʃtɔf]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-Sauerstoff.ogg|Audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Sauerstoff.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Sauerstoffs|-|gen2=Sauerstoffes}}

# [[oxygen]]

====Usage notes====
* '''Sauerstoff''' [[tanken]] - to breathe fresh air (to go outside and "tank oxygen")

====Synonyms====
* {{l|de|Atemluft}} (breathing air)

